                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Recommended: It's a dollar. What the hell do you want?\n\nThis game is objectively stupid, and I mean that in the most affectionate way possible.\n\nThe gameplay loop is about as deep as a puddle in the Jurassic Park parking lot. You start a level, shoot some raptors, fight a bigger dinosaur, unlock more guns, and repeat until either the dinosaurs are extinct again or your brain starts to smooth out.\n\nThere's no groundbreaking gameplay here. No compelling narrative. No revolutionary mechanics. Just you, a growing collection of firearms, and dinosaurs that apparently didn't get the memo about staying extinct.\n\nBut here's the thing: the game knows exactly how stupid it is.\n\nFor the low, low price of ONE AMERICAN DOLLAR, you get this magnificent exercise in prehistoric mediocrity AND a staggering 1,079 Steam achievements. That's not a typo. One thousand and seventy-nine. That's more achievements than the game has reasons to exist.\n\nAnd the achievements? They're arguably the best part. Most are hilarious, and some are literally letters of the alphabet in different styles, allowing you to spell out words on your Steam profile. That's right, for less than the price of a gas station hot dog, you get a mediocre dinosaur shooter AND the ability to decorate your profile with whatever dumb shit you can spell.\n\nIs the game repetitive? Absolutely.\n\nIs it shallow? Like a kiddie pool in a drought.\n\nWill you get bored? Almost certainly.\n\nDid I have fun? Against all reasonable expectations, yes.\n\nThis isn't a hidden gem. It's a shiny piece of gravel, and the developers are fully aware they're selling gravel. But it's a dollar, the dinosaurs explode, the achievements are funny, and somehow the whole ridiculous package works.\n\n10/10 for knowing exactly what it is.\n\n4/10 as an actual video game.\n\nWould absolutely waste another dollar.",
